@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+## Summary
+
+B-044: the HUD keeps clear of the right-hand controls. The board and mirror fits are untouched (`place()` never sees hudRects).
+
+- `rightPadRects` (joined_view.dart): dpad/gyro = faceButtons + start; sticks = faceButtons + rightStick (rightZone when floating) + start; screen px with the bar shift. Passed as `FrameView.hudRects`.
+- `HostPad.hudRects` (host_overrides.dart): `_hostHudRects`, the same rects moved up by `topBarHeightPx`; "Show on this device" stays empty.
+- camera.dart: `hudPlace` rejects a beside-world form that meets a hudRect inflated by `mirrorGapPx`; `mirrorPlace` takes `hudRects` and passes them to both its `hudPlace` calls only; dartdoc says so. camera_fit.dart: `_hudUnder` takes hudRects, moves right of one it meets, and rejects overlap. match_view.dart passes `hudRects` to `mirrorPlace`.
+- Tests (new): controller_app/test/right_pad_rects_test.dart (8 mode/size cases + host hudRects); packages/puzzle_game/test/hud_place_right_controls_test.dart (3 tests).
+- Seen: tools/mine.sh ok (47 controller_app tests, 4 puzzle_game tests, analyze clean). The named existing tests pass: controller_app 14, puzzle_game 26.
+- Tests-first: I did not run the new tests against the old code. They would not compile or would fail there, because `rightPadRects` and the `hudRects` parameter of `mirrorPlace` did not exist.
+
+## Computed values
+No numeric expectations; checks are geometric (inside box, no overlap with left rects, clear of the inflated hudRect, equality with and without a far hudRect).
+
+## Decisions
+- The 1640x2360 hudPlace test builds the control rect from where the free HUD lands, because that spot depends on the layout; it needs no fixed pixel value.
+- The test that hudRects don't change the world is done through `mirrorPlace` (place() has no such parameter), with a far rect leaving rect, scale and hud unchanged.
+- `hudPlace` with a mirror (short form only) that meets a hudRect falls through to the corner, which stays as the last place.
+
+## Self-check
+1. Host setups: host hudRects test (phone host, dpad); show-on-device unchanged (empty, existing mirror_pad_test case).
+2. No new kept state.
+3. No pause/away/dropped-link state touched.
+4. Stayed inside allow:.
+5. No stop needed.
+6. Sizes: right_pad_rects_test at 1640x2360 and 852x393, every mode. The HUD stays a fraction of the box.
+
+## Hand-over
+Device check: whether the HUD sits well beside the A/B/X/Y ring on the iPad in portrait.
+
+## Commit message
+
+m165 b1s: HUD keeps clear of the right-hand controls (B-044)
+
+rightPadRects maps the X/Y/A ring, right stick and Start/Pause as rects.
+The joined view and the host's HostPad.hudRects pass them on. hudPlace,
+mirrorPlace and _hudUnder keep the clock area clear of them with
+mirrorGapPx of air. place(), the board fit and the mirror fit are unchanged.
+
+## Status row
+
+m165 b1s: HUD clears the right-hand controls (rightPadRects, hudRects in hudPlace/_hudUnder/mirrorPlace); open: device check on the iPad in portrait.
+
+## Delete
+
+- none
